** Deconstruct
	Is used for extracting any class properties .
	Used for returning multiple values from a method (like Tuple)
	
	Ex:-
		class Point
			{
				public int X { get; }
				public int Y { get; }

				public Point(int x, int y) { X = x; Y = y; }
				public void Deconstruct(out int x, out int y) { x = X; y = Y; }
			}

			(var myX, var myY) = GetPoint(); // calls Deconstruct(out myX, out myY);
			or
			var (myX, myY) = GetPoint();
			or 
			(var myX, _) = GetPoint(); // when only myX is required and myY is not required
	
	Advantage:- We can define multiple overloaded methods for returning n no. of outouts. Hence we can costumise our logic as well.
	
** Local functions
	Any function defined inside another function is called Local function.
	Ex:-
		public int Fibonacci(int x)
			{
				if (x < 0) throw new ArgumentException("Less negativity please!", nameof(x));
					return Fib(x).current;  // local function is called and tupil property is "current" is being used
					
				 //local function defination
				(int current, int previous) Fib(int i)
					{
						if (i == 0) return (1, 0);
							var (p, pp) = Fib(i - 1);
						return (p + pp, p);
					}
			}
	
	
	
** yield :- 
		Used when any value needs to be returned without exiting method execution. Example getting fibonacci series.

static IEnumerable<int> GenerateFibonacciNumbers(int n)

       {

           for (int i = 0, j = 0, k = 1; i < n; i++)

          {

               yield return j; // will return j as and when control hits this line

               int temp = j + k;

               j = k;

               k = temp;

           }

       }
	   
main()
{	   
	foreach (int x in GenerateFibonacciNumbers(10)) // x is yield value

   {

       Console.WriteLine(x);

   }
}   

