** Return ref     variable from function
	When a function returns a referential variable, it returns address of that variable not value.
	Ex:-
		public ref int Find(int number, int[] numbers)
		{
			for (int i = 0; i < numbers.Length; i++)
				{
					if (numbers[i] == number) 
					{
						return ref numbers[i]; // return the storage location, not the value
					}
				}							
		}

		ref int place = ref Find(7, array); // aliases 7's place in the array
		int[] array = { 1, 15, -39, 0, 7, 14, -12 };
		place = 9; // replaces 7 with 9 in the array
		WriteLine(array[4]); // prints 9
		
** Easiest way to throw exception
	Ex:- class Person
			{
				public string Name { get; }
				public Person(string name) => Name = name ?? throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(name));
				public string GetFirstName()
					{
						var parts = Name.Split(" ");
						return (parts.Length > 0) ? parts[0] : throw new InvalidOperationException("No name!");
					}
				public string GetLastName() => throw new NotImplementedException();
							
			}
    
--------------------------- C# 6.0--------------------------------
** Expression builder method:- new way of writting method body in one line.
	Ex:- public int CalculateMonthlyPay(int dailyWage) => dailyWage * 30;

** Conditional access :- now null check for object is not needed with conditional access.
	Ex:- string employeeMiddleName = employee?.EmployeeProfile?.MiddleName ?? "N/A";
	(if any property is null, variable will be initialized with "N/A", instead of getting exception)

** Auto property initializer: any referential property can be directly initialized while defining a 
			      class. Hence get, set is not needed.
	Ex:- class PeopleManager
		{
   			public List Roles { get; } = new List() { "Employee", "Managerial"};
		}

** Primary constructor :- when we pass parameters to class at declaration label, is called primary constructor.
	Ex:- class Basket(string item, int price)
		{   
   			public string Item { get; } = item;
  			 public int Price { get; } = price;
		} // mainly this concept is used for auto property initialization

**Out parameter declaration dusring method call:- Out parameter is now not needed to be defined separately.
		It can be defined while calling a method.
	Ex:- int.TryParse(value, out int convertedValue) 

** Await in catch block:- now await can be implemented in catch block to have async calls
